From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Oct 2026 19:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: on PS5, say which process publishes which display rate

With PROTON_120HZ=1 a program in the Mihawk OS session was offered only 60 Hz modes although its own
WINE_PS5_REFRESH was 120 (PS5_Proton's modes-p2-2026-10-17-02; the same probe as the initial program in the probe
prefix was offered 60 and 120). Every process that first takes the desktop window publishes the driver's mode from its
own environment, and the last one wins; one line per publish names the rate, the variable and the native process, so a
run shows which one published 60.
---
 dlls/win32u/ps5drv.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/dlls/win32u/ps5drv.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/ps5drv.c
@@ -237,6 +237,11 @@
                          NtUserGetSystemDpiForProcess( NULL ), param );
     manager->add_monitor( &monitor, param );
     manager->add_modes( &mode, 1, &mode, param );
+    /* Which process publishes which rate: every process that first takes the desktop window publishes from its own
+     * environment, and the last one wins (PS5_Proton's docs/PLAN.md, modes-p2-2026-10-17-02) */
+    fprintf( stderr, "wine-ps5: display published %ux%u@%u Hz (WINE_PS5_REFRESH=%s) by native process %d\n",
+             (UINT)mode.dmPelsWidth, (UINT)mode.dmPelsHeight, (UINT)mode.dmDisplayFrequency, refresh ? refresh : "unset",
+             (int)getpid() );
     return STATUS_SUCCESS;
 }
 
